<title>POLAND: Most Polish minimum T-bill prices fall, 13-wk rise. [CORRECTED 13:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Most Polish minimum T-bill prices fall, 13-wk rise. [CORRECTED 13:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.2 billion zlotys against a 900 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 772 (corrects from 712) million zlotys of the bills.  </p>
<p>  T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---    95.51    91.17     ---     83.55</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---   (95.50)  (91.18)    ---    (83.56)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---    95.57    91.22     ---     83.63</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---   (95.58)  (91.24)    ---    (83.65)</p>
<p>   offer		---    200.0    100.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---    405.8    132.5     ---     661.0</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---    200.0     99.3     ---     473.0</p>
<p>   next auction     ---    200.0    200.0     ---     550.0</p>
<p>   (Corrects accepted bids of 52-week T-bills from 413 to 473)</p>
<p>NOTE: Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
